@startuml credential-lifecycle
title Credential lifecycle
skinparam shadowing false

state "Active" as Active
state "Refresh due" as RefreshDue
state "Expired" as Expired
state "Revoked" as Revoked

[*] --> Active : all requirements met\n(issue, copy unlocks)
Active --> RefreshDue : notice period before valid_until reached,\nor a policy version requires a refresher
RefreshDue --> Active : refresher completed\n(update unit, full run or test,\nper qualification)
RefreshDue --> Expired : valid_until plus grace period passed
Expired --> Active : refresher completed
Active --> Revoked : admin revokes (audited)
RefreshDue --> Revoked : admin revokes (audited)
Expired --> Revoked : admin revokes (audited)
Revoked --> [*]

note right of Active
  The credential names the tasks it unlocks.
  It carries no score and no rank.
  Qualifications with validity_kind none
  only leave Active through an event or a revocation.
end note
@enduml
